Bundled Vim runtime files
=========================

These files are copied into root's ~/.vim by the vim module. Only files
that Vim 9 does not already ship are bundled here; Vim 9 detects *.pp and
*.epp on its own and provides its own markdown and less.vim support, so
there are no ftdetect files and no copies of Vim's own runtime.

Source: https://github.com/rodjek/vim-puppet
Commit: 21b2b9ecaf8ef18ea4755ed7f82937eb97989c82 (2026-04-08)
License: Apache-2.0 (same as this module)

Files taken verbatim from that commit:

  after/ftplugin/puppet.vim    aligns hashrockets as you type =>
  autoload/puppet/align.vim    used by after/ftplugin/puppet.vim
  autoload/puppet/format.vim   used by ftplugin/puppet.vim (formatexpr)
  ftplugin/epuppet.vim
  ftplugin/puppet.vim
  indent/puppet.vim
  syntax/epuppet.vim
  syntax/puppet.vim

Deliberately not taken: ftdetect/ (Vim 9 detects these filetypes),
autoload/puppet/ctags.vim, ctags/, ftplugin/puppet_tagbar.vim,
after/plugin/gutentags.vim, compiler/, ftdetect/puppet.lua and test/.
These need developer tooling (ctags, tagbar, gutentags, puppet-lint,
neovim) that does not belong in a server default.

To update, see "Updating the bundled vim files" in AGENTS.md.
